# An extractor works its deposit and produces the deposit's density, not one.
#
# **This is the whole point of a deposit.** Every rule so far produces a number written into the
# rule; this one produces a number read out of the world, which is what `spec/data/line.4x` writes
# as `$where`'s density for that resource.
#
# **Red on purpose.** Nothing declares a `work` rule, and no clause can yet take a quantity from a
# row an earlier clause matched.

{test name:an-extractor-pulls-its-deposits-density}

{given}
{territory id:1}
{density where:1 what:5 quantity:6}
{extractor where:1 for:5 quantity:1}
{residency what:2 where:1 quantity:1}

{when}
{work where:1 for:5}

{then}
{territory id:1}
{density where:1 what:5 quantity:6}
{extractor where:1 for:5 quantity:1}
{residency what:5 where:1 quantity:6}
